From 96c3c142178907586356002f7e3ca5dac30cea9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:41:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LOOM-8: the harmonizer. A track can follow the conductor's
 chord, not just its scale: the conductor now keeps the chord its keys, its
 steps or a FOLLOW track play (up to four notes, packed in one word the
 interrupt reads whole), and the new follow modes "harmony" (each note snaps
 to the nearest chord tone, register kept, ties down) and "chord deg" (the
 note's place in the scale picks the chord tone, kept in its octave) take
 their pitches from it. A single-note source is its diatonic triad; a scene
 re-derives the triad from its degree; no chord falls back to diatonic. Fills
 keep their chord tones. Five follow modes in the SEL lists and the routing
 page (a bar marks the harmonizer's), the active chord shown on the
 conductor's Engine page. No format change: the two modes are appended values
 of TP_BRAIN. harmony.xy; t_harmony; the manual

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
